duate study), its shift toward non-portfolio creative-business courses, and its entry requirements for Indian students -- roughly 55% for Foundation/Postgraduate and 65% for Undergraduate -- alongside scholarships of GBP 2,000 or more.","children":[{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:08/session:2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university/topic:vernon-street","title":"Vernon Street","level":"topic","summary":"","children":[],"evidence":{"sessionRef":"2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university","sessionRefs":["2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university"]}},{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:08/session:2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university/topic:blenheim-walk","title":"Blenheim Walk","level":"topic","summary":"","children":[],"evidence":{"sessionRef":"2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university","sessionRefs":["2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university"]}},{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:08/session:2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university/topic:indian","title":"Indian","level":"topic","summary":"","children":[],"evidence":{"sessionRef":"2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university","sessionRefs":["2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university"]}},{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:08/session:2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university/topic:foundation","title":"Foundation","level":"topic","summary":"","children":[],"evidence":{"sessionRef":"2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university","sessionRefs":["2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university"]}},{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:08/session:2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university/topic:postgraduate","title":"Postgraduate","level":"topic","summary":"","children":[],"evidence":{"sessionRef":"2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university","sessionRefs":["2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university"]}},{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:08/session:2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university/topic:gbp","title":"GBP","level":"topic","summary":"","children":[],"evidence":{"sessionRef":"2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university","sessionRefs":["2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university"]}},{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:08/session:2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university/org:the-outreach-collective-toc","title":"The Outreach Collective (TOC)","level":"org","summary":"","children":[],"evidence":{"sessionRef":"2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university"}}],"evidence":{"sessionRef":"2026-08-24-uniaccess-leeds-arts-university"}},"score":0,"reason":"The document discusses entry requirements and scholarships for Indian students at Leeds Arts University but does not mention anything about UK student visas."},{"node":{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:04/session:2026-04-21-visa-blueprint-part2-italy-france-nz","title":"Visa Blueprint Part 2: Italy, France, New Zealand","level":"session","summary":"TOC hosted three destination specialists to walk counselors through student-visa mechanics for New Zealand, France, and Italy. Kshitij Garg (Estero Education) covered New Zealand's fully online e-visa process, its 76% 2025 approval rate against a 27,000-by-2030 target, and the rule that only nationalized-bank secured loans (never NBFC or unsecured loans) satisfy Immigration New Zealand's proof-of-funds test. Shagun Handa (Campus France) explained the Classes Internationales pathway (capped at EUR 5,500) and the two-year APS post-study permit for Master's graduates. Ruby Thomas (Uni-Italia) detailed Italy's strict three-tier document legalization chain, where a Sub-Divisional Magistrate (SDM) stamp is explicitly rejected in favor of the university-to-state-HRD-to-MEA apostille sequence.","children":[{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:04/session:2026-04-21-visa-blueprint-part2-italy-france-nz/topic:new-zealand","title":"New Zealand","level":"topic","summary":"","children":[],"evidence":{"sessionRef":"2026-04-21-visa-blueprint-part2-italy-france-nz","sessionRefs":["2026-04-21-visa-blueprint-part2-italy-france-nz","2026-07-30-in-focus-3"]}},{"node_id":"toc/year:2026/month:04/session:2026-04-21-visa-blueprint-part2-italy-fran